<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="hero">
  <div>
    <span class="pill">Software for HR teams managing migrant-worker permits</span>
    <h1><%= co.PRODUCT_NAME %><br><small>Automate reports, document downloads and form filling in Thailand's e-WorkPermit system</small></h1>
    <p class="lead">A Windows application that does the repetitive clicking in the Department of Employment's e-WorkPermit portal for you:
      pull hundreds of application statuses into Excel, download receipts and appointment slips in bulk, and fill BT.30 / BT.44 forms straight from a spreadsheet.
      You pay only for the records actually processed.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a href="/contact" class="btn primary big">Open an account</a>
      <a href="/pricing" class="btn big">See pricing</a>
      <a href="/portal/login" class="btn big">Customer login</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="shot"><img src="/hero.jpg" alt="<%= co.PRODUCT_NAME %> application screenshot" loading="lazy" onerror="this.parentNode.style.display='none'"></div>
</section>

<section id="features" class="features">
  <h2>What the software does</h2>
  <div class="grid3">
    <div class="feat"><div class="ic">📊</div><h3>Reports and data extraction</h3>
      <p>Pull application lists from e-Tracking by application type, status and date range, including worker details and officer remarks, into Excel.
      Works across many accounts in one run. Also permit application reports, worker name lists and Ticket ID checks.</p></div>
    <div class="feat"><div class="ic">📥</div><h3>Bulk document downloads</h3>
      <p>Receipts, BT.44 / BT.22 / BT.53 / BT.55 / BT.52 / BT.56 forms, result notices, application receipts, payment slips, acknowledgements and appointment slips,
      named by passport number and sorted into folders automatically. Re-runs skip files that already exist.</p></div>
    <div class="feat"><div class="ic">✍️</div><h3>Form filling from Excel</h3>
      <p>Worker registration, employer notification (BT.52), MoU renewal (BT.30) and employer change (BT.44) filled from a spreadsheet,
      with a dry-run mode that stops before submission and a confirmation prompt before any step that carries a government fee.</p></div>
    <div class="feat"><div class="ic">📅</div><h3>Real-time appointment slot checker</h3>
      <p>Scans available dates and time slots for card-photo appointments at every branch, with an auto-refreshing monitor window.</p></div>
    <div class="feat"><div class="ic">🔒</div><h3>Your data stays on your computer</h3>
      <p>The software runs on your own PC with your own e-WorkPermit login. Reports and PDFs are saved locally.
      We only receive usage statistics (operator, mode, record count, time) for billing — never your password or worker data.</p></div>
    <div class="feat"><div class="ic">📈</div><h3>Transparent usage</h3>
      <p>Every job is logged. Review usage per operator, per mode and per month in the customer portal before you are invoiced.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="how">
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><b>Open an account</b> — send us your operator name and email via the contact page; we set up your free account within 1 business day.</li>
    <li><b>Install</b> — download the installer and setup guide from your email. Windows 10/11, unlimited machines.</li>
    <li><b>Use it</b> — enter your operator name in the app, pick a mode and press Start. The software records how many items it processed.</li>
    <li><b>Get invoiced monthly</b> — on the 1st we issue an invoice for the previous month's usage × unit prices. Pay via Lemon Squeezy in the portal; the receipt arrives by email instantly.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section id="pricing" class="pricing">
  <h2>Pricing</h2>
  <p class="lead">No setup fee, no minimum, no contract. You pay for the records actually processed. Invoices are issued on the 1st of each month and paid via Lemon Squeezy.</p>
  <p class="center"><a href="/pricing" class="btn primary">See unit prices per task →</a></p>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="faq">
  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <details><summary>Is this a document-processing service?</summary><p>No. It is <b>software</b> that you install and operate yourself with your own e-WorkPermit account. We never access your account or file anything on your behalf.</p></details>
  <details><summary>How is usage billed? What counts as a "record"?</summary><p>1 record = 1 application / 1 document / 1 worker processed successfully in a given mode. Unit prices differ per mode (see <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a>). Jobs cancelled midway are billed only for what was completed. On the 1st of each month we issue an invoice for the previous month, payable via Lemon Squeezy in the customer portal.</p></details>
  <details><summary>What do I need?</summary><p>Windows 10/11, Python 3.12 or newer (installer provided), a working e-WorkPermit account and an internet connection.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is there a contract?</summary><p>No. No card on file, no automatic charges. If you stop using the software, there is no invoice for that month — only invoices for months already used remain payable. See the <a href="/refund">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Who issues the receipt?</summary><p>Lemon Squeezy is the Merchant of Record, so it issues the receipt and handles sales tax. Your card statement will show Lemon Squeezy. You can add your company name, address and tax ID to the receipt.</p></details>
  <details><summary>Is our data safe?</summary><p>Your password and worker data never leave your computer. The software sends us only usage statistics for billing. Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p></details>
</section>

<section class="contactcta">
  <h2>Questions, or want a trial first?</h2>
  <p>Email <% if (co.COMPANY_EMAIL) { %><a href="mailto:<%= co.COMPANY_EMAIL %>"><%= co.COMPANY_EMAIL %></a><% } %>
     <% if (co.COMPANY_PHONE) { %> · call <%= co.COMPANY_PHONE %><% } %> or <a href="/contact">send us a message</a> (<%= co.SUPPORT_HOURS %>)</p>
</section>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
